Subject: Walnut memory defaults: no hardware acceleration, no page cache,
 WebGL or WebRTC

For the PS3's 256 MB of RAM. Hardware acceleration policy NEVER keeps GL out of the web process: on
a PC (WebKitGTK 2.54, the GameDB home page) it took the web process from 218 to 90 MB PSS, nearly
all of a tuned shell's saving; Cairo on big-endian rasterises on the CPU anyway, and the policy
makes sure no GL context is made. WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 (unless set already) keeps GBM
and EGL out of the UI process (24 MB on the PC). No back/forward page cache (WebKit sizes it at 0
on a machine this small anyway), no WebGL, WebRTC or media stream, no smooth scrolling (one repaint
per scroll step on a slow CPU), no developer extras unless WALNUT_BROWSER_DEVTOOLS=1.

Run-time overrides for measuring: WALNUT_BROWSER_ACCEL=never|ondemand|always,
WALNUT_BROWSER_CACHE=browser|viewer (the cache model; BADWOLF_CACHE_MODEL in config.h is the
default) and WALNUT_BROWSER_MEMORY_LIMIT=<MB> (WebKit's memory pressure limit, for the network
and the web processes; WebKit's default is the RAM size).

