+/* Walnut (256 MB of RAM, an in-order CPU, a GL 2.1 GPU): the settings above leave out what costs
+ * memory or CPU time on every page. Hardware acceleration NEVER keeps GL out of the web process (on
+ * a PC it cut that process from 218 to 90 MB); no back/forward page cache (going back reloads, from
+ * the disk cache); no WebGL, WebRTC or camera; no smooth scrolling (one repaint per step); the
+ * inspector only with WALNUT_BROWSER_DEVTOOLS=1.
+ *
+ * BADWOLF_CACHE_MODEL: WEBKIT_CACHE_MODEL_WEB_BROWSER (memory and disk caches) or
+ * WEBKIT_CACHE_MODEL_DOCUMENT_VIEWER (no disk cache, no cached processes).
+ * Run-time overrides, for measuring: WALNUT_BROWSER_ACCEL=never|ondemand|always,
+ * WALNUT_BROWSER_CACHE=browser|viewer, WALNUT_BROWSER_MEMORY_LIMIT=<MB> (WebKit's memory pressure
+ * limit; the default is the RAM size), WALNUT_BROWSER_DEVTOOLS=1.
+ */
+#define BADWOLF_CACHE_MODEL WEBKIT_CACHE_MODEL_WEB_BROWSER
+
